# Phase 18 Producer nullable queue-filter mapping — 2026-10-14T03:27:00Z

- Continued `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`; pinned RocketMQ Java client remains `5.5.1` at `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`, and its checkout remains read-only.
- Added invoked Java 5.5.1 `TopicPublishInfo.selectOneMessageQueue(QueueFilter...)` cases for null and empty filter arrays, null elements with nonempty/empty/null queue lists, and filter evaluation order when the first filter returns false. Java returns no queue in the last case but still evaluates the next filter because `filterResult &= ...` is non-short-circuiting.
- Added `TopicPublishInfo::select_one_message_queue_with_nullable_filters`, a nullable filter callback type, and `NullPublishInfoQueueFilter`; the existing closure-slice method now delegates to the nullable implementation. Added a Rust differential test and updated the Phase 7 Producer matrix and release checklist.
- Code/test/fixture commit: `96f7c8d1` (`feat(producer): map nullable queue filters`). Fixture SHA-256: `d8e0fb04555fa9e730277d2230f37b48eb0ae159f9f49610d96eff3c369de051`.

